{"record_id":"D19-B99-R004","dataset_id":"D19","dataset_version":"1.0","batch":"B99","topic":"Security Engineering","subtopic":"Whole-Dataset Quality Assurance","concept":"D19 residual-gap register","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","question":"Why should remaining security knowledge gaps be explicitly recorded before lock?","answer":"A dataset can be broad without being complete. Explicit residual gaps prevent the absence of records from being mistaken for absence of required knowledge and create a controlled basis for future version updates.","rule":"Every material known gap must be recorded with scope, impact, rationale, and disposition rather than hidden by declaring completion.","verification_method":"Compare D19 scope against the coverage matrix and produce a residual-gap register before lock.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"NOT_VALIDATED","evidence_level":"INTERNAL_DATASET_GOVERNANCE","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":["Autonomous Software Engineering Brain dataset governance specification"],"relationships":["D19-B90-R005","D19-B98-R005","D19-B99-R001"]}

{"record_id":"D19-B99-R005","dataset_id":"D19","dataset_version":"1.0","batch":"B99","topic":"Security Engineering","subtopic":"Whole-Dataset Quality Assurance","concept":"D19 lock decision evidence","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","question":"What evidence is required for a defensible D19 lock decision?","answer":"The lock decision should reference the final dataset version, schema validation, coverage audit, deduplication results, contradiction review, provenance review, implementation audit, test and verification linkage, execution-status audit, relationship validation, residual-gap register, and known limitations.","rule":"LOCKED is a governance state supported by an audit record, not a conclusion inferred from reaching B100.","verification_method":"Verify that the lock report contains all required audit dimensions and that each reported status is supported by actual evidence.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"NOT_VALIDATED","evidence_level":"INTERNAL_DATASET_GOVERNANCE","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":["Autonomous Software Engineering Brain dataset governance specification"],"relationships":["D19-B90-R005","D19-B99-R001","D19-B99-R002","D19-B99-R003","D19-B99-R004"]}

{"record_id":"D19-B100-R001","dataset_id":"D19","dataset_version":"1.0","batch":"B100","topic":"Security Engineering","subtopic":"Final Dataset Completion","concept":"D19 scope-completion audit","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","question":"What must the final D19 scope-completion audit establish?","answer":"It must establish that the defined Security Engineering scope has been covered across security foundations, threat modeling, authentication, authorization, secrets, validation, injection, cryptography, serialization, secure errors, web/API security, transport security, filesystem/process security, dependencies, concurrency, supply chain, protocol security, service trust, resource exhaustion, recovery, evidence, privacy, and integrated assurance, while identifying any explicitly accepted residual gaps.","requirements":["Scope coverage","Concept coverage","Failure coverage","Implementation applicability audit","Testing coverage","Verification coverage","Version awareness","Provenance","Residual-gap register"],"constraints":["Do not equate record count with completeness","Do not silently rewrite prior records","Do not fabricate missing evidence"],"verification_method":"Compare the authoritative D19 scope map with the complete record graph and produce a signed/versioned completion report.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"NOT_VALIDATED","evidence_level":"INTERNAL_DATASET_GOVERNANCE","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":["Autonomous Software Engineering Brain dataset governance specification"],"relationships":["D19-B99-R004","D19-B99-R005"]}

