{"record_id":"D20-B47-R002","dataset_id":"D20","dataset_version":"1.0","topic":"Test Generation","subtopic":"Oracle Construction","concept":"Generated-test oracle validation","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","question":"Why must generated test oracles be validated independently?","answer":"A generated expected result can reproduce the same reasoning or defect as the implementation, producing false confidence.","principle":"Test generation and oracle generation should be sufficiently independent to provide useful evidence.","failure_mode":"The generated test accepts the same incorrect behavior as the implementation.","root_cause":"Oracle was derived from the implementation without an independent specification or invariant.","testing_guidance":"Prefer independent properties, reference implementations, metamorphic relations, or manually reviewed expected behavior where appropriate.","verification_method":"Assess the oracle's independence and trace it to an authoritative requirement or independent reasoning source.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PRACTICE","confidence":"HIGH","relationships":["D20-B28-R005","D20-B47-R001"],"provenance":["established testing and oracle-design practice"]} 
{"record_id":"D20-B47-R003","dataset_id":"D20","dataset_version":"1.0","topic":"Test Generation","subtopic":"Mutation Guidance","concept":"Mutation-guided test generation","knowledge_type":"TECHNIQUE","question":"How can mutation results guide test generation?","answer":"Surviving mutations can identify behavioral changes that existing tests fail to distinguish, providing targeted evidence about missing assertions, inputs, or scenarios.","requirements":["Generate meaningful mutations","Run relevant tests","Identify surviving mutations","Map each survivor to missing test evidence","Add or revise tests where justified"],"constraints":["Mutation survival can have legitimate explanations","Mutation scores do not by themselves establish correctness"],"verification_method":"Verify that a new test kills the intended mutation without relying on incidental implementation details.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PRACTICE","confidence":"HIGH","relationships":["D20-B10-R002","D20-B47-R001","D20-B06-R003"],"provenance":["mutation-testing literature","established mutation-testing practice"]} 
{"record_id":"D20-B47-R004","dataset_id":"D20","dataset_version":"1.0","topic":"Test Generation","subtopic":"Regression Generation","concept":"Defect-to-regression transformation","knowledge_type":"CODE_TRANSFORMATION","question":"How should a confirmed defect become a regression test?","answer":"Convert the smallest reproducible failure condition into a test that fails on the defective behavior, passes on the corrected behavior, and remains linked to the defect evidence.","procedure":["Preserve original failure","Minimize reproducer","Define expected invariant","Implement regression test","Verify it distinguishes defective and corrected behavior","Link evidence and test"],"failure_mode":"The regression test passes before the fix or does not distinguish the defect from unrelated behavior.","root_cause":"The test does not encode the actual failure condition.","verification_method":"Run against the defective or simulated pre-fix behavior and corrected behavior where safely reproducible.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PRACTICE","confidence":"HIGH","relationships":["D20-B05-R003","D20-B44-R004","D20-B06-R004"],"provenance":["established regression-testing practice"]} 
{"record_id":"D20-B47-R005","dataset_id":"D20","dataset_version":"1.0","topic":"Test Generation","subtopic":"Deduplication","concept":"Generated-test deduplication","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","question":"How should redundant generated tests be detected?","answer":"Generated tests should be compared by semantic purpose, input domain, oracle, covered behavior, and failure-detection capability rather than only by textual similarity.","principle":"Two syntactically different tests can provide the same evidence.","failure_mode":"Large generated suites contain many near-duplicate tests that add little diagnostic or coverage value.","root_cause":"Deduplication operates only on source text.","testing_guidance":"Retain distinct edge cases and independent oracles while removing semantically redundant cases.","verification_method":"Compare the behavior and evidence contribution of candidate duplicate tests.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PRACTICE","confidence":"HIGH","relationships":["D20-B47-R001","D20-B30-R001"],"provenance":["D20 quality-first dataset governance","established test engineering practice"]}

{"record_id":"D20-B48-R001","dataset_id":"D20","dataset_version":"1.0","topic":"Test Repair","subtopic":"Automated Repair","concept":"Test repair safety","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","question":"When is automated test repair potentially unsafe?","answer":"Automated repair is unsafe when it changes assertions or test intent merely to restore a passing result without evidence that the underlying requirement or expected behavior changed.","failure_mode":"A failing regression test is weakened until it passes without correcting the product defect.","root_cause":"Pass status is optimized instead of preserving the test's intended oracle.","testing_guidance":"Require requirement or contract evidence for changes to expected behavior.","verification_method":"Compare the repaired test with the original requirement, defect evidence, and intended invariant.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PRACTICE","confidence":"HIGH","relationships":["D20-B01-R005","D20-B47-R004","D20-B06-R004"],"provenance":["established test-maintenance practice"]} 
