{"record_id":"D20-B51-R001","dataset_id":"D20","dataset_version":"1.0","topic":"Formal and Model-Based Testing","subtopic":"State Models","concept":"State-machine test derivation","knowledge_type":"PROCEDURE","question":"How can a state model be used to derive software tests?","answer":"A state model can derive tests by representing valid states, events, guards, transitions, and expected state invariants, then generating or selecting paths that exercise required transition behavior.","requirements":["Define states","Define events","Define transition guards","Define transition effects","Define state invariants"],"constraints":["The model may omit real implementation behavior","Model correctness must be evaluated independently","Generated paths should be selected according to coverage objectives"],"procedure":["Construct the behavioral model","Identify required transitions and invariants","Generate candidate paths","Select paths according to risk and coverage","Execute tests","Compare observed behavior with the model"],"failure_mode":"The implementation behaves outside the modeled transition contract or the model itself encodes incorrect assumptions.","root_cause":"Mismatch between implementation behavior and authoritative behavioral specification, or an inaccurate model.","testing_guidance":"Include valid transitions, invalid transitions, repeated events, boundary states, recovery states, and terminal states.","verification_method":"Verify model-to-requirement traceability and confirm that selected tests exercise the intended transitions.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PRACTICE","confidence":"HIGH","relationships":["D20-B02-R005","D20-B07-R005","D20-B47-R001"],"provenance":["established model-based testing practice","ISO/IEC/IEEE 29119 testing concepts"]}

{"record_id":"D20-B51-R002","dataset_id":"D20","dataset_version":"1.0","topic":"Formal and Model-Based Testing","subtopic":"State Models","concept":"Invalid transition testing","knowledge_type":"TEST_CASE","question":"Why should state-machine tests include invalid transitions?","answer":"Invalid transition tests verify that operations are rejected, ignored, or otherwise handled according to the contract when invoked from states where they are not permitted.","requirements":["Define invalid operations per state","Define expected rejection or handling","Verify state preservation or specified transition"],"failure_mode":"An operation succeeds from an unauthorized or invalid state and creates an inconsistent system state.","root_cause":"State validation is missing, incomplete, or incorrectly ordered.","testing_guidance":"Attempt prohibited transitions from representative states and verify both externally visible behavior and resulting state.","verification_method":"Check that each invalid transition produces the documented outcome without violating state invariants.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PRACTICE","confidence":"HIGH","relationships":["D20-B07-R001","D19-B14-R001","D20-B51-R001"],"provenance":["established state-machine testing practice"]}

{"record_id":"D20-B51-R003","dataset_id":"D20","dataset_version":"1.0","topic":"Formal and Model-Based Testing","subtopic":"State Models","concept":"Transition coverage versus state coverage","knowledge_type":"COMPARISON","question":"What is the difference between state coverage and transition coverage?","answer":"State coverage asks whether relevant states have been reached; transition coverage asks whether relevant state changes have been exercised. A suite can cover every state while missing important transitions between them.","principle":"State presence does not establish transition behavior.","testing_guidance":"Track both state and transition coverage when the model's transition behavior is contractually important.","verification_method":"Compare the executed transition graph with the required model graph.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PRACTICE","confidence":"HIGH","relationships":["D20-B10-R001","D20-B51-R001"],"provenance":["established model-based testing practice"]}

