{"record_id":"D20-B88-R002","dataset_id":"D20","dataset_version":"1.0","topic":"Advanced Verification Testing","subtopic":"Verification composition","concept":"Common-mode verification failure","knowledge_type":"FAILURE_MODE","question":"What is a common-mode verification failure?","answer":"A common-mode verification failure occurs when multiple verification mechanisms share the same incorrect assumption, defective oracle, data source, or implementation dependency and therefore fail together.","failure_mode":"Independent-looking checks produce the same incorrect conclusion because their evidence is correlated.","solution":"Introduce genuinely independent evidence sources or explicitly model the shared dependency.","verification_method":"Trace verification artifacts to common assumptions, code paths, specifications, and data sources.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PRACTICE","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":["Verification assurance principles","Fault-tolerance and independence concepts"],"relationships":["D20-B86-R002","D20-B88-R001","D20-B44-R001"]} 
{"record_id":"D20-B88-R003","dataset_id":"D20","dataset_version":"1.0","topic":"Advanced Verification Testing","subtopic":"Verification composition","concept":"Evidence confidence versus correctness","knowledge_type":"DISTINCTION","question":"Why should verification confidence be distinguished from correctness?","answer":"Confidence describes the strength and completeness of available evidence under stated assumptions, whereas correctness is the property being established; high confidence does not justify claiming correctness beyond the evidence scope.","principle":"Evidence strength and truth status must remain separate fields in a verification knowledge system.","verification_method":"Store evidence_level, confidence, verification scope, and unresolved conditions independently.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PRACTICE","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":["Evidence-based verification practice"],"relationships":["D20-B10-R005","D20-B44-R001","D20-B85-R005"]} 
