{"record_id":"D20-B93-R002","dataset_id":"D20","dataset_version":"1.0","topic":"Implementation-Oriented Testing","subtopic":"Invalid implementation testing","concept":"Incorrect retry test","knowledge_type":"INVALID_CODE","objective":"Demonstrate a retry test that accidentally hides persistent failure.","incorrect_code":"for _ in range(5):\n    try:\n        operation()\n        break\n    except Exception:\n        pass\nassert True","failure_mode":"All failures can be swallowed and the test still passes.","symptom":"A permanently failing operation produces a passing test result.","root_cause":"The test does not preserve or assert the final failure state.","corrected_code":"last_error = None\nfor _ in range(5):\n    try:\n        operation()\n        break\n    except Exception as error:\n        last_error = error\nelse:\n    raise AssertionError(\"operation failed after retries\") from last_error","testing_guidance":"Retries may help diagnose transient behavior but must not convert unresolved failure into success.","verification_method":"Inject a deterministic persistent failure and verify that the test fails rather than passing.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PRACTICE","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":["Flaky-test and retry testing principles"],"relationships":["D20-B05-R004","D20-B45-R003","D20-B44-R001"]} 
